From 219986ef1971362752a3f2f847f06c165c5d488d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 06:48:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore: optimize Claude Code config for tokens, context &
 model routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

settings.json:
- model: opus[1m] -> sonnet (cheaper default; promote to opus via /model)
- effortLevel: high -> medium (per-skill effortLevel still overrides)
- env: add CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=haiku, DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1
- permissions: drop duplicate "Edit" and phantom "Update"
- enabledPlugins: disable chrome-devtools-mcp, claude-code-setup,
  code-simplifier (overlaps built-in /simplify); keep claude-hud
  enabled because the statusLine command depends on its plugin dir

CLAUDE.md:
- replace "always use agent teams" rule with a default-to-single-agent
  rule; teams reserved for 3+ parallelizable units of work
- drop @RTK.md auto-import (RTK is invoked transparently by the
  rtk-rewrite hook); leave a one-line pointer instead

skills:
- discovery/define/architecture: model: opus + effortLevel: high
  (design trio kept on the strongest reasoner — these run rarely
  per-feature so the cost is bounded)
- build/implement: model: sonnet (mechanical; escalate via /model)
- review: model: sonnet + effortLevel: high (lead stays Sonnet,
  documented /review --deep escape hatch for opus on risky PRs)
---
 CLAUDE.md                    |  7 ++++---
 settings.json                | 16 ++++++++--------
 skills/architecture/SKILL.md |  2 ++
 skills/build/SKILL.md        |  1 +
 skills/define/SKILL.md       |  2 ++
 skills/discovery/SKILL.md    |  3 ++-
 skills/implement/SKILL.md    |  1 +
 skills/review/SKILL.md       |  2 ++
 8 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md
index ac34d56..b1166bd 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -4,8 +4,9 @@ This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with co
 
 ## Implementation Rules
 
-- **Always use agent teams** for non-trivial implementation. Use `TeamCreate` to spawn teammates — assign each a separate sub-issue or file group to avoid conflicts. Only fall back to single-agent for trivial single-file fixes. When dispatching subagents, explicitly instruct them to use teams.
-- Respond concisely; no filler, no preamble
+- **Default to single-agent.** Use `TeamCreate` only for parallelizable work across 3+ independent files or sub-issues. Team overhead (per-agent system prompt, message passing, coordination) costs more than it saves on smaller tasks.
+- Respond concisely; no filler, no preamble.
+- Use the cheapest viable model. Skills set their own `model:` and `effortLevel:` — trust them.
 
 ## Feature Workflow
 
@@ -51,4 +52,4 @@ The `scripts` command is globally available (linked from `~/Projects/scripts`).
 
 Run `scripts --help` or `scripts <command> --help` for details on available commands and options.
 
-@RTK.md
+RTK reference: `~/.claude/RTK.md` (read on demand — RTK is invoked transparently by the `rtk-rewrite.sh` PreToolUse hook).
